    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70-a1">

                <pb facs="0143" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg109"/>

                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to the Prince de la Tour d’Auvergne.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 28, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Washburne, minister of the United States, presents his respectful compliments
                    to the Prince de la Tour d’Auvergne, and begs leave to inclose him herewith,
                    copies of two dispatches which have just been transmitted to him by Mr. Motley,
                    the minister of the United States at London, and which explain themselves.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
